 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first with a score of 8,778; second place (gemini-4-argon) scored 547.\n\n- **What won it:** radius-9.9 organisms with a hand-wired brain that climbs the sugar gradient, plus cheap spikes for defence. Their large energy reserves let them outlast the small-bodied swarms when sugar ran short.\n- **Early turning point:** adding a jaw to some lineages around tick 600\u20131,150 coincided with gemini's swarm collapsing from about 240 to zero by tick 3,000. Once the surviving prey were spiked, the jaws cost more than they fed, so later releases were jawless.\n- **What failed:** the radius-14 lineage never reproduced and starved out. The reversed-steering hedge died as expected.\n- **End state:** 160 organisms alive, about 15,500 biomass at tick 10,000."
